nl.statement:
Can one compute, exactly and in time polynomial in \(n\) in the fixed-dimensional exact-real model, the original sharp summary-inversion image
\[
\mathcal C_{n,\alpha}
=\{\overline F(q):q\in\mathcal K,\ d_S(q,\Pi(\widehat S_n))\le2r_{n,\alpha}\}
\]
and its exact support-dependent cluster extrema, without compact nearest-summary optimization or black-box evaluation of \(\overline F\)?  The positive real law estimator \(\widehat\lambda_n\), the honest outer set \(\mathcal C^{\mathrm{alg}}_{n,\alpha}\), and every interval in its report \(\mathfrak R_{n,\alpha}\) now have explicit fixed-dimensional constrained representations, including when the raw empirical operator has nonreal eigenpairs.  The remaining question concerns an exact or sharp polynomial-time algorithm for the original summary-inversion image and its extrema, not the existence of an evaluable confidence set or report.

nl.frozen_body:
Let \(P_{g,h}\) be the factorization-preserving two-class path law of \cref{obj:def:path-law-family}. Suppose that
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Gap range.)} \(0\le g\le 1/4\).
\item \textbf{(Tangent amplitude.)} \(|h|\le 1/100\).
\end{itemize}
Then \(P_{g,h}\) satisfies the proxy-rank margin in \cref{obj:ass:proxy-rank-margin} with proxy-rank singular-value margin \(\sigma_0=1/10\): the reference-proxy feature matrices \(A_0\) and \(A_1\) from \cref{obj:def:reference-feature}, and the target-proxy feature matrix \(B\) from \cref{obj:def:target-feature}, all formed from \(P_{g,h}\), have smallest singular value at least \(1/10\).

Let \(P\) be a full-data probability law carrying \((U,T,X,Z,Y(0),Y(1),Y)\), and let \(\pi_0>0\). Suppose \(P\) satisfies latent-arm positivity with margin \(\pi_0\), as in \cref{obj:ass:latent-arm-positivity}. Then, for each treatment arm \(t\in\{0,1\}\), the diagonal matrix
\[
\Gamma_t
=
\operatorname{diag}\left\{
\frac{P(U=u,T=t)}{P(T=t)}
: u\in\{1,\ldots,k\}
\right\}
\]
defines an injective linear map on \(\mathbb R^k\).

nl.statement:
Let \(Q\in\mathcal M\) with observable summary \(S(Q)\), and write \(G:=\operatorname{stack}(M_0(S(Q)),M_1(S(Q)))\) and \(s_0=\pi_0\sigma_0^2\).  Then there exist an orthonormal basis \(V\) spanning the stacked signal row space of \(S(Q)\) and a real diagonalization of the compressed effect operator \(\Delta Q(Q)\) such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(\operatorname{rank}(G)=k\);
\item for every index \(j\), \(s_0/2\le\sigma_j(G)\) if and only if \(j<k\);
\item for each arm \(t\in\{0,1\}\) the compressed map \(x\mapsto M_t(S(Q))Vx\) is injective;
\item the eigenvalues of the diagonalization are the latent-class treatment effects \(\tau_u(Q)\), \(1\le u\le k\);
\item the left spectral anchor \(a(Q)^\top\) carries the latent-class masses \(p_u(Q)\) in the diagonalizing coordinates, and the right spectral anchor \(c(Q)\) is carried to \(\mathbf 1_k\).
\end{enumerate}
